# Applies to `server/Dockerfile`'s build context, which is the REPO ROOT (the
# image needs `packages/` and `server/` as npm workspace members plus the
# root package.json/lockfile) -- Docker resolves a Dockerfile-specific
# ignorefile named `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` relative to the context
# root in preference to a plain `.dockerignore`, which is what lets this file
# live at `server/Dockerfile.dockerignore` and still govern a repo-root
# context without a root-level `.dockerignore` affecting unrelated builds
# (e.g. `engine/Dockerfile`'s own `context: engine`).
#
# Allowlist form (exclude everything, then re-include only what the build
# stage actually COPYs) rather than enumerating every large directory to
# exclude -- the repo root also holds ios/, engine/, relay/, .git/, none of
# which this image needs, and a missed one would silently balloon the build
# context and leak dev-only files (`.env*`, `server-secrets.json`) into a
# build layer.
#
# `desktop/` IS needed (re-included below): `npm -w desktop run build:web`
# (spec 18) builds the browser Studio client that this image serves at
# `server/web/` behind `server.json.web.enabled` (spec 11). Only the source
# tree is needed, not desktop's own node_modules/dist -- the re-excludes
# below already strip those from every re-included workspace.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!packages
!packages/**
!server
!server/**
!desktop
!desktop/**

# Re-exclude dev/build artifacts and secrets that would otherwise be pulled
# back in by the `!server/**` / `!packages/**` re-includes above.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.git
**/*.log
**/logs
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/server-secrets.json
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
